From 9ccb41bbde40354da96c70ca3b7b1b23837158c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:37:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ci: drop HEGEL_ENGINE_VERSION, which nothing reads

The workflow set HEGEL_ENGINE_VERSION to v0.17.4 and described it as the
engine pin.  No step, Makefile or script reads it: the engine job builds
the deps/hegel submodule, and the pin is LIBHEGEL_VERSION in the Makefile
(0.50.0).  A comment says where the version comes from instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019ndjvrCDpVjyeVdC5cqgPz
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 7ede5b6..33ab41c 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -9,11 +9,9 @@ on:
   pull_request:
     branches: [main]
 
-# Engine (libhegel.so) source version.  Pinned to the tag local dev
-# builds from and the runtime is verified against (see CLAUDE.md).
-# Bump deliberately — CI then builds and tests the exact engine dev uses.
-env:
-  HEGEL_ENGINE_VERSION: v0.17.4
+# The engine (libhegel.so) version is not set here: the `engine` job builds
+# whatever deps/hegel is checked out at, which the release watch keeps on
+# the Makefile's LIBHEGEL_VERSION tag (see CLAUDE.md, "libhegel").
 
 jobs:
   # Build the engine cdylib (libhegel.so) from source once and share it.
-- 
